00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.152
Why. hello there.
boys and girls.

3
00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:31.114
We'd like to introduce you
to a dying breed.

4
00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.743
This is Joseph "KP" Simmons.

5
00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:36.995
otherwise known as Joe.

6
00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:42.584
Joe was born in 1937 and is 89 years old.

7
00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.963
He is what one might call
an endangered Negro species.

8
00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.549
They certainly don't make them
like this anymore.

9
00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:54.179
As a matter of fact.
Joe was even once a pimp.

10
00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:56.097
Doesn't he look swell?

11
00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:58.141
Why a pimp. you ask?

12
00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:02.187
Well. Joe only received
a third-grade education.

13
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.108
and with his extremely limited vocabulary.
he couldn't work at Amazon.

14
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:09.944
For instance.
in what you're about to witness.

15
00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:11.905
he says the word "motherfucker."

16
00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:15.992
or in his colloquial language.
"muthafucka."

17
00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:19.412
approximately 76 times.

18
00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:23.792
He says the word "pussy"
approximately 24 times.

19
00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:28.296
He says the n-word approximately 74 times.

20
00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:34.177
And he throws in an occasional "bitch"
and "ho" at random. for good measure.

21
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.388
So if you're sensitive
to these types of words.

22
00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:40.683
you may want to turn
to more wholesome programming.

23
00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.894
but you won't laugh as hard.

24
00:01:42.977 --> 00:01:47.524
Yes. boys and girls.
get ready to watch an old-school Negro.

25
00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.319
A man stuck in time
when women couldn't vote

26
00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:54.239
and were constantly objectified by men.

27
00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:59.410
A man who has no idea
that the world around him has changed.

28
00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:02.455
A man who says anything
that comes to his mind.

29
00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:05.708
and I do mean anything.

30
00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.919
Does this sound like someone you may know?

31
00:02:08.002 --> 00:02:11.339
Sit back. relax. and please

32
00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:15.426
brace yourselves
for the antics of a dying breed.

33
00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:34.949
-Hey. Steve and Brenda. how are you?
-Hi. Brian.

34
00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:36.749
-Good to see you.
-You too!

35
00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:40.034
-Karen. Chad. great to see you.
-How's it going?

36
00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:41.518
-Good to see you.
-Afternoon.

37
00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:49.919
♪ I've got a graduate
Gonna be an empty nester ♪

38
00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.837
Come on.

39
00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.339
-B.J.?
-I mean… I know.

40
00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.051
B.J.! Hey. Todd. Stewart.
I didn't know you guys were here.

41
00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.219
-How are you?
-Hey. Dad.

42
00:02:58.303 --> 00:02:59.137
Hey. Mr. Simmons.

43
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.431
-What are you guys huddling about?
-Ah…

44
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.974
-Well…
-Nothing. Nothing. really.

45
00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:05.393
B.J. just got another offer
from another school.

46
00:03:05.476 --> 00:03:06.311
Oh. that's great!

47
00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:08.897
I wouldn't really call it a school.
It's more like crap.

48
00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.481
-It's Morehouse.
-Thank you.

49
00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:11.941
-Whoa. hold on.
-Thank you.

50
00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:15.528
Morehouse is a great school.
It's one of the finest HBCUs there is.

51
00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.322
-What are you talking about?
-Uh…

52
00:03:17.405 --> 00:03:19.699
HBCU. what is that?

53
00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:24.037
HBCU. Historically Black
college and university.

54
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.760
Okay. Dad.

55
00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:27.373
Wait. hold on. What am I missing?

56
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.126
Thanks. Dad. but no thanks.
Look. really. it's fine.

57
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.586
No. what am I missing. really?

58
00:03:32.295 --> 00:03:37.091
Okay. it's kind of funny. actually.
because we were just talking about this.

59
00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:40.220
-Why is there a need for Black colleges?
-Yeah.

60
00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:42.722
I mean. really. what's the point?

61
00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:45.183
-I mean. it's kind of racist. right?
-Yeah.

62
00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:46.392
It's racist?

63
00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:48.895
Yeah. like a little bit against us.

64
00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:50.939
I mean. you don't look around and see

65
00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:53.775
historically white colleges
and universities. do you?

66
00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:54.776
Yeah. you do.

67
00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:58.905
Every university is a historically white...
What are you saying? What's happening?

68
00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:01.950
-Come on. Dad. Seriously…
-You guys are pranking me. seriously.

69
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.136
Dad. don't tell me
you really subscribe to this stuff.

70
00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.203
-I mean...
-Hold on.

71
00:04:05.286 --> 00:04:08.498
Dr. Martin Luther King
went to Morehouse. huh?

72
00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.751
Okay. we will give you
the benefit of the doubt.

73
00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:16.297
but I'm sure that this type of institution
was important at some point.

74
00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:17.821
-Hm.
-Necessary. even.

75
00:04:17.882 --> 00:04:19.550
-But the world's changed now.
-Hm.

76
00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:22.804
-A lot's happened. We're all equal.
-Yeah.

77
00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:26.432
And all this baggage
about civil rights and slavery…

78
00:04:26.516 --> 00:04:28.017
-"Baggage"?
-Woe is me!

79
00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.937
I mean. you gotta let it go at some point.
Like. it was in the past.

80
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.607
Exactly. Hey. you know.
aren't we all equal under the law?

81
00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:38.278
You know what?
When I was coming. I forgot to tell you.

82
00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:40.201
Your dad's calling you.
your mom's calling you.

83
00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:42.448
They want you home.
B.J.. I need to talk to you.

84
00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:44.117
-I didn't get a call.
-That's weird.

85
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.619
-No. I'm fine. Dad.
-B.J.. I need to talk to you.

86
00:04:46.703 --> 00:04:48.246
Oh. no. No. there's no need to.

87
00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:50.290
because I've actually decided
to go to Pepperdine.

88
00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:51.853
Yeah. with my pals.

89
00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.167
And get this.

90
00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:56.462
They're gonna drive across country with me
to go do a campus visit next week.

91
00:04:56.546 --> 00:05:00.049
-Road trip! Let's go!
-Gonna be awesome! California!

92
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.467
-Woo-hoo!
-Yes!

93
00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:04.637
-Let's go plan the charging stations now.
-You're right.

94
00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:07.223
-I didn't even think about that! Let's go!
-Yes!

95
00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.559
Yeah! We're going to California. boys!

96
00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.560
California!

97
00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:14.480
-We're going to California.
-Yeah! Woo! California dreamin'!

98
00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:15.857
Yeah! Woo!

99
00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.568
What the hell did I do?
This is not good.

100
00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.321
B.J.. can we just…?

101
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:35.626
Hey. hey. Hey.

102
00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.754
Hey. there. come on in here.

103
00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.548
You want some cabbage? Come on in.

104
00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:45.178
Oh. is that what that smell is. huh?
No. I'm gonna pass on that. How you doing?

105
00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:46.661
When I used to come home from work.

106
00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:48.556
I didn't know if that was from cooking

107
00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:50.433
or her up there trying to wash her...

108
00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.393
Joe. shut the hell up.

109
00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.103
What bring you by here? Look at you.

110
00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.356
Oh. Madea. wow. You look... You look nice.

111
00:05:56.439 --> 00:05:58.316
You know damn well she don't look nice.

112
00:05:58.399 --> 00:06:01.194
Come up here talking about she look…
Shut up. Shit.

113
00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:03.071
I look good as hell all the time.

114
00:06:03.154 --> 00:06:04.739
All the time. I look good as hell.

115
00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:06.699
Shut the hell up. Thank you. Joe.

116
00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:07.658
Hm.

117
00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:10.203
All right. go on. tell me.
what the hell you kids do now.

118
00:06:10.286 --> 00:06:13.456
Nothing. I just wanted to come over
and say hi to both of you.

119
00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:15.949
No. they done something.

120
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.360
He only come over here
when them damn children do something.

121
00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:20.856
Look. I'm too damn old
to be trying to pull things out of you.

122
00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.131
Go on ahead and tell me. hell.

123
00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:25.176
Fine. You know.
B.J.'s going off to college. and…

124
00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:28.805
You know. I walked in on him having
the most interesting conversation.

125
00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.933
He was sitting with
his little white friends. and they were…

126
00:06:32.016 --> 00:06:36.145
That's the problem right there.
He got all them damn clear friends.

127
00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.814
What are you talking about?

128
00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.357
He mean "white."

129
00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.360
Okay. all right. clear. I get it. okay.

130
00:06:42.443 --> 00:06:45.154
But you know that
I did not raise him to see race.

131
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.198
Here this nigga go
with this stupid shit.

132
00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:50.910
You might not have raised him to see race.
but when the police look at him.

133
00:06:50.993 --> 00:06:52.870
they gonna see a straight-up nigga.

134
00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:54.789
Can I finish?

135
00:06:54.872 --> 00:06:56.457
Do we have to let you finish?

136
00:06:56.541 --> 00:06:58.459
Okay. so as I said.
I walked in on them.

137
00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:01.254
and they're having this conversation
about colleges. right?

138
00:07:01.337 --> 00:07:04.400
And he was telling me he doesn't see
the need for a historically Black college.

139
00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.258
Say what?

140
00:07:05.341 --> 00:07:07.301
He wants to go to Pepperdine
in Malibu.

141
00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:11.472
Yeah. Then he went on to talk about
how Black people need to get over slavery.

142
00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:13.808
Can you believe that?
He said. "Get over slavery."

143
00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:16.352
And the Civil Rights Movement.
Then he said. "baggage."

144
00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.354
I was like. "What is wrong with this kid?"

145
00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.898
I don't even know what's wrong with him.

146
00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.318
What? Why are you two so quiet?

147
00:07:24.402 --> 00:07:26.779
Boy. you send that boy to all-clear.

148
00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:29.157
all-white. all-damn-day school.

149
00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.575
In Georgia.

150
00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:34.078
He been the only damn Black face
up in there since he was a kindervagarber.

151
00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:36.414
And you wonder
why he think like that. Shit.

152
00:07:36.497 --> 00:07:39.000
All them clear people
done cleared out all his Black thoughts.

153
00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:41.169
All right. but all white people
don't think that way.

154
00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:43.754
Listen here. I told you not to send him
to that damn P-school.

155
00:07:43.838 --> 00:07:45.882
You know what "P"
in the private stand for?

156
00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:48.885
It ain't for "private."
It's for "pussy." Pussy school.

157
00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:51.554
Joe. hush that.
Don't be saying that word up in here.

158
00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:56.058
You got that boy walking around here
like he a big. huge. orange FUPA.

159
00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:58.394
He said. "FU…".

160
00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:02.231
He said. "FUPA." You know what that is?
That big. fat. upper…

161
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.149
Never mind.

162
00:08:03.232 --> 00:08:06.402
Mabel know what a FUPA is.
Mabel got a dupa.

163
00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.739
And you done spent all that money
sending that boy to the private school.

164
00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:12.658
and they done took every book
about a Negro out of there.

165
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:14.452
-Didn't they. Joe?
-You damn right.

166
00:08:14.535 --> 00:08:17.663
Took every...
Ain't a book about Sojourner The Truthers.

167
00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:22.460
They took out Moses. Mayola. everybody.
Not even Maya Angelou.

168
00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:24.921
Not even in the room.
They don't have Maya Angelou.

169
00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:28.108
She's not in there.
That's just wrong. Took all the books out.

170
00:08:28.132 --> 00:08:32.970
Ain't nothing wrong with a public school.
I graduated from a pub… Well…

171
00:08:33.054 --> 00:08:34.934
I ain't quite grad...
I went to a public school.

172
00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.558
And Joe went to a public school too.
Hell. look how we turn out.

173
00:08:37.642 --> 00:08:39.393
You damn right I went to public school.

174
00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:42.063
I went to public school all my life.
all the way through.

175
00:08:42.146 --> 00:08:44.815
I graduated all the way
from the third grade.

176
00:08:44.899 --> 00:08:47.459
B.J. wasn't the toughest kid.
He wasn't tough like you two. okay?

177
00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:49.820
I didn't want him to go to a public school
and be bullied.

178
00:08:49.904 --> 00:08:52.281
Oh. you didn't? Oh. well. congratulations.

179
00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:55.159
You kept him from being bullied.
That's... Congratulations.

180
00:08:55.243 --> 00:08:58.246
You also kept the little motherfucker
from being Black. Congratulations.

181
00:08:58.329 --> 00:09:00.665
You a great Black dad.
Great Black dad keep his Black kids

182
00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:02.917
from being Black
so he don't know if he's Black or not.

183
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.378
That's a good job. son. Good job.

184
00:09:05.461 --> 00:09:09.006
Okay. hold on. There's nothing wrong
with me not wanting my kid to be bullied

185
00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.469
or beat down. or "Meet me at 3 o'clock."
like you guys used to do all the time.

186
00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.096
There's nothing wrong with that. okay?

187
00:09:15.179 --> 00:09:16.847
I just wanted him to go to a nice school.

188
00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:19.952
and didn't want him to feel like he was
at a disadvantage because he's Black.

189
00:09:19.976 --> 00:09:22.228
Nigga. he is at a disadvantage.

190
00:09:22.311 --> 00:09:23.896
-You know that. hell.
-Right.

191
00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.649
Whenever you see a Black man
with an even playing field?

192
00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:29.086
And if you say sports.
I'mma come up there and grab that pot

193
00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.990
and burn you with
whatever the hell she cooking.

194
00:09:31.028 --> 00:09:33.173
Don't threaten my cabbage.
I gotta finish this cabbage.

195
00:09:33.197 --> 00:09:34.740
Don't burn him with this damn cabbage.

196
00:09:34.824 --> 00:09:37.868
You know why she like to eat cabbage?
She wanna cover up what she smell like.

197
00:09:38.452 --> 00:09:41.497
Listen. I know that it's not fair
out there for some of us.

198
00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:42.915
Did he say. "Some of us"?

199
00:09:42.999 --> 00:09:44.834
He did. Brian. let me ask you something.

200
00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:47.295
Did you ever have "the talk" with him?

201
00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:49.297
No. No. no. no. I didn't.

202
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.465
But hold on.
before you jump down my throat.

203
00:09:51.549 --> 00:09:55.094
It hurts to have to talk to your kid
about all we went through as Black people.

204
00:09:55.177 --> 00:09:56.387
So. so…

205
00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.556
I did not wanna tell him right away. okay?

206
00:09:58.639 --> 00:10:01.726
I just wanted to wait
a little while till he got older.

207
00:10:01.809 --> 00:10:03.978
and I didn't think
any of this would happen.

208
00:10:04.061 --> 00:10:05.941
Congratulations.
You ain't said a thing.

209
00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.150
But what you have to understand
is you ain't got to tell him all at once.

210
00:10:09.233 --> 00:10:10.513
Tell him a little bit at a time.

211
00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:13.380
That should've started when he was young.
so he know who the hell he is.

212
00:10:13.404 --> 00:10:16.164
Right. Remember. he didn't want you
to go to that school and tell him.

213
00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:18.200
"Put them books back in."
He was embarrassed by it.

214
00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:19.285
I remember that.

215
00:10:19.368 --> 00:10:22.121
Only reason you let me go to that school
is it was the last resort

216
00:10:22.204 --> 00:10:23.404
when you called me over there.

217
00:10:23.456 --> 00:10:26.096
I went there to pick that boy up
from school that day you couldn't.

218
00:10:26.167 --> 00:10:27.335
You know what they was doing?

219
00:10:27.418 --> 00:10:29.086
They was out playing on the playground.

220
00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.758
They had took all the asphalt
up out the ground and put down carpet.

221
00:10:33.841 --> 00:10:35.468
There was green carpet.

222
00:10:35.551 --> 00:10:39.263
What kind of shit is that? I was playing
on bottles and broken mattresses...

223
00:10:39.347 --> 00:10:41.015
Them mattresses was so damn disgusting.

224
00:10:41.098 --> 00:10:44.518
but you'd bounce on them and get stuck.
whatever had you sticking to it.

225
00:10:44.602 --> 00:10:47.396
But we played on them.
That's some real learning right there.

226
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.648
They…

227
00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:51.233
They don't want the kids
to hurt themselves on asphalt.

228
00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:52.443
so they put the carpet...

229
00:10:52.526 --> 00:10:54.362
Joe. I'm getting ready to stab him.

230
00:10:54.445 --> 00:10:57.365
I told you he's gonna be a little bitch.

231
00:10:57.448 --> 00:10:59.075
